  {
    "episode_id": 71132,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71132.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Hi, Kate. Yeah. So I got to interview the Milwaukee Democrat, Gwen Moore, about some priorities for Black History Month. We kind of talked in general about what Black Milwaukeeans need most and how the government can accomplish those issues. But I also wanted to make sure I touched on some of the major issues more deals with in her day to day life as a Congresswoman since she has represented Wisconsin's majority black district since 2004. Thank you so much, Congresswoman Gwen Moore, for joining me on today's podcast. I really appreciate having you on the show today.",
