    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71132.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Well, I can tell you that the first African Americans came to Wisconsin in like the 1700s. I mean, I think we've even seen where an African American signed the charter for the city of Milwaukee. We belong here. We're part. of the history of this state, you know, along with our brothers and sisters and Native Americans and the early immigrants. And we shouldn't take a back seat to anybody. We deserve healthcare. It ought to be all right. We deserve an educational opportunity and an effort to overcome the deindustrialization and move to be retrained and educated and skilled because we came here to work. We migrated from the South to work. We didn't come here for a handout. We want to be educated. We want healthcare. And we want decent housing to live in, just like everybody else. And we're willing to work for it. And we belong here. We are part of Black History in Wisconsin.",
